        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.448,
            0.809,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look at Fig. 8.12 and try to answer the following questions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.476,
            0.768,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) How many red squares are there in Stages 0 to 3?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.503,
            0.883,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Can you predict the number of red squares in Stages 4 and 5?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.53,
            0.886,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Can you find a rule for the number of red squares at the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " stage? Write the explicit formula as well as the recursive formula for the number of red squares at any stage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.598,
            0.886,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Suppose the area of the square in Stage 0 is 1 square unit. What is the area of the red region in Stages 1, 2 and 3? What will be the area of the red region in Stages 4 and 5? Find the explicit as well as the recursive formula for the area of the red region at the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " stage. What happens to this area as n, the number of stages, goes on increasing?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.304,
            0.765,
            0.692,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "End-of-Chapter Exercises"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.809,
            0.885,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the 31"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "st",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of an AP whose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 1 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is 38 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 6 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is 73."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.854,
            0.886,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Determine the AP whose third term is 16 and whose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
